<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soon May the Wellerman Come</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Soon May the Wellerman Come&quot;, also known as &quot;Wellerman&quot; or &quot;The Wellerman&quot;, is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> folk song in ballad style. Its title refers to the &quot;wellermen&quot;, the supply ships of the Weller brothers and the men who worked for them. Edward, George and Joseph Weller were British-born merchants who had emigrated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney-nova-scotia">Sydney</a> in 1829.</p></div>
